# Round-5 DT-OPS-21 fix : Python proto stubs are generated at build
# time from `protos/efe/v1/*.proto` (see `clients/python/Makefile`
# target `proto`). Committing them caused silent drift between the
# `.proto` source and the generated `.py` consumed by tests — code
# review never saw the regeneration step. The next commit touching
# these proto definitions should run `make -C clients/python proto`
# and rely on this rule to keep the artifacts out of git.
clients/python/efe_tool/_proto/efe/v1/*_pb2.py
clients/python/efe_tool/_proto/efe/v1/*_pb2.pyi
clients/python/efe_tool/_proto/efe/v1/*_pb2_grpc.py
